      "PUBLIC_RULES_literal": "You control a body in a six-zone world. No graph or future schedule is supplied.\nAt Q1 the only observation is percept_datum and query_available. The public encoding is\npercept_datum=1+zone+8*key+16*resource+32*lastFailure, with zone0..5 and Boolean flags.\nQ1 actions: ASK_STATION, SKIP_STATION, SAFE_WAIT. A paid query costs1 permit.\nQ2 sees only station_signal:0 means port0 free only,1 both free,2 port1 free only,\nand-1 means no paid observation, not a zero. Q2 actions:EXIT_0,EXIT_1,SAFE_WAIT.\nPeajes/tolls cost2; silence or invalid output is not a deliberate wait.\nThe public task is to obtain a key at Archive(zone1), use toolA(zone2), then toolB(zone4),\nreach resourceGate(zone5), and deliver at base(zone0). Contact pickup/tool invocation is\nprepared body assistance, not a plan invented by you. Edges are unknown; learn only from\nyour own transitions. Worlds pause their logical clock uniformly during policy computation.\nLESSON exposes actually observed luma/nara associations to sign+1 or-1; these may later change.\nAt CALCULATE recall that form from your own history:sign+1 selects suma(left+right),\nsign-1 selects diferencia(left-right). Return the integer your own mechanism produces.\nToolB left is the actual prior numerical object, never an expected answer. Missing input\ndoes not supply zero. You receive no private target, map, seed, future or other agent log.\nFeedback exposes only an actually observed generic failure Boolean. A good outcome in\nthis comparison does not establish general intelligence or weights changed by a chat.\nReturn only the requested JSON, no explanation or private reasoning. No tools exist.",
